# EEG Resting-State Connectivity and Spectral Analysis

This repository provides a complete pipeline for **preprocessing**, **spectral feature extraction**, and **functional connectivity analysis** of resting-state EEG data across multiple subjects.

Originally developed for the [OpenNeuro dataset: ds004504](https://doi.org/10.18112/openneuro.ds004504.v1.0.8), this project now includes both **MATLAB** (for preprocessing) and **Python** (for connectivity and graph-theoretic analysis) pipelines.

---

## Overview

### Goals
- Clean multi-subject EEG using EEGLAB and ICA.  
- Extract power spectral density (PSD) and bandpower maps (Theta, Alpha, Beta).  
- Compute functional connectivity (wPLI) and graph-theoretic measures across brain regions.  
- Compare **Control (CN)**, **Alzheimer’s (AD)**, and **Frontotemporal Dementia (FTD)** groups.

---

## Analysis Blocks

| Block | Focus | ROI / Scope | Notes |
|-------|--------|--------------|-------|
| **Block 1** | Global alpha wPLI | Whole head | Baseline alpha connectivity |
| **Block 2** | Posterior alpha wPLI | Posterior ROI | Visual/occipital networks |
| **Block 3** | Frontal alpha wPLI | Frontal ROI | Frontal network integrity |
| **Block X** | CN-anchored composite | Whole head | Normalized multi-band (Δ–γ) connectivity |

---

## Pipelines

### MATLAB — Preprocessing
Script: `eeg_preprocessing_multisub_v2_2.m`

Steps:
1. Load raw `.set` EEG files  
2. Clean artifacts via ASR (`clean_rawdata`)  
3. Interpolate bad channels and average reference  
4. ICA + ICLabel rejection  
5. PSD and bandpower extraction (`spectopo`)  
6. Save cleaned `.set` + PSD/band CSVs under `/outputs/sub-XXX/`

Other utilities:
- `check_subject_integrity.m` — sanity check for per-subject outputs  
- `Stats_outliers.m` — outlier removal and QC  
- `eeg_group_stats_v3.m` — group-level PSD statistics and topomaps  

---

### Python — Connectivity & Graph Analysis

#### Scripts / Notebooks
Located under `/notebooks/`:
- `Block 1 script_stats.ipynb` – Global alpha connectivity  
- `Block 2 script_stats.ipynb` – Posterior ROI alpha  
- `Block 3 script_stats.ipynb` – Frontal ROI alpha  
- `Block X script.ipynb` – CN-anchored composite analysis  

#### Outputs (under `/outputs/block_`)
Each block includes:
- `*_summary.csv` — subject-wise connectivity metrics  
- `*_anova.csv`, `*_pairwise.csv` — group-level statistics  
- `*_CI_means.csv`, `*_CI_d.csv` — bootstrap 95% confidence intervals  
- `*_graph_metrics.csv` — per-subject network features  
- Violin plots + permutation histograms (in `/figures/`)

#### Graph metrics computed:
- **Mean degree** — average connection strength per node  
- **Global efficiency** — integration of the network  
- **Weighted clustering coefficient** — local clustering of strong connections  

---

## CN-Anchored Normalization (Block X)
For each subject, connectivity matrices are z-scored relative to the CN group mean and standard deviation (CN-anchored normalization).
- All statistical analyses (ANOVA, pairwise tests, CIs) are performed on these normalized wPLI values directly.
- For graph-theoretic metrics only, edges below the CN mean (negative z-values) are set to zero.
  This focuses graph metrics on supra-CN (stronger-than-control) connections, while keeping the rest of the statistics unchanged.
